17592186489642} {:answer/id #uuid "41956628-242f-5bff-a74b-494fa731d555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/497d1c67fb3a322ae402f6dfa69c8b069d91177ddef6a5847e6dbee4cb93f995.png" :db/id 17592186489664} {:answer/id #uuid "a20e0b6e-d6c8-5746-bf51-509b5c8a9a60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/18/18d9c0adc10639219feaca56d61376d5be64b5b49535c2a92a55f6e5d3422832.png" :db/id 17592186489875} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe1a0f0-9239-5016-8995-7682b6c6771b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/0400a1437f26b74feb16161cf51a88c175ee6837fe1e5d8f8785ba2bb2b9c68b.png" :db/id 17592186489932} {:answer/id #uuid "d90bc894-c41c-5fae-ad3b-1cd61eefe589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cc/cc985bf7790c1e8b6ec01ecc4b9bcde1c47073591ce02eef867ed652632a819c.png" :db/id 17592186489992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfe1a0f0-9239-5016-8995-7682b6c6771b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/0400a1437f26b74feb16161cf51a88c175ee6837fe1e5d8f8785ba2bb2b9c68b.png" :db/id 17592186489932} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a58be1d-9b02-526d-a31b-cb5a653e1224" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186490116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60940cd3-550d-521c-8bf6-1906baac5be6" :question/math-academy-id "q-71695" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x+2.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x+2.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=2(0)+2=2,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)+2=4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)+2=6,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)+2=8.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane: \n\n![](images/6b/6b2da4bfc7c768788d143999fb61e76bb3a60facffc35e430d98085b395932f7.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of  $y=2x+2.$\n\n![](images/04/0400a1437f26b74feb16161cf51a88c175ee6837fe1e5d8f8785ba2bb2b9c68b.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Line Using a Table"}
